<h2>Segment 222 &mdash; the deed after cessation</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s222S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w1">las de</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w2">byas pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s222w4">skad cig</span> gnyis par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w5">zhig</span> na <span class="u particle" data-d="6" data-l="s222w6">ni</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w7">mtshams de nas</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w8">&#x27;bras bu dngos su &#x27;byin pa&#x27;i snga logs kyi bar du</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w9">las de</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w10">med</span> la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w11">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w12">zhig pa</span> yang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w13">dngos por</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w14">med</span> pas <span class="u" data-d="2" data-l="s222w15">las las &#x27;bras bu ji ltar &#x27;byung bar &#x27;gyur</span> zhes <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w16">brtsad pa</span>&#x27;i lan du</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s222S">From the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s222w4">moment</span> after</span> you <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w2">complete</span> a karma or deed, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w1">that deed</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w5">finished and gone</span>. During the entire period <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w7">from that point</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w8">up to the point at which the consequence actually occurs</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w9">the deed</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w10">no longer exists</span>. A <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w11">deed</span> which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w12">already gone</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w14">no longer</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w13">thing</span> that can have any affect on anything. <span class="u" data-d="2" data-l="s222w15">How then does a deed or karma ever produce any kind of consequence?</span> Here is how we explain this <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w16">problem</span>:<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s222w6"><span class="nul">Emphatic topic marker after the conditional na; the English presents the topic by clause structure and punctuation without a separate particle exponent.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Codex reconciliation; PROVISIONAL machine alignment. The initial las de owns that deed once, preserving de's explicit demonstrative; the earlier karma or deed repeats that participant and stays outside. HGM attests skad cig gnyis pa as the moment after/second moment; its unique skad cig member owns moment, while gnyis par is not falsely made an independent after. Both zhig occurrences are cessation predicates; finished and gone and already gone retain their complete lexical readings. ni is emphatic topic marking without a separate English particle; the conditional na is omitted because the English recasts this premise as an assertion. The complete temporal endpoint is d3: Tibetan has the giving forth of a consequence with karma implicit as giver, English has the consequence occur. This is the same endpoint event, but 'byin pa is not equated atomically with occurs. The two med occurrences own no longer exists and no longer; the latter's copular frame is distributed around thing. dngos por owns thing; the functional explanatory relative clause remains outside. The complete final reported question is d2: consequence arising FROM deed is recast as deed producing consequence, preserving cause and result without a false atomic 'byung bar/produce pair. lan du is distributed across Here is how we explain and omitted; brtsad pa owns problem. The affect/effect wording is retained verbatim and separately flagged as a LOW/PROBABLE English copyedit for human source review; no source text is corrected.</div>
